ffmpeg-dmo (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Carry two of the edition's own FFmpeg pull requests, both approved in
    review, on top of the frame_packing series of +stereo3d11 (ORDER 425):
    - FFmpeg pull request 25409 (https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/25409),
      patches 0069 and 0070: the SEI payload type and size read by
      ff_h264_sei_decode() are bounded before the sum can pass INT_MAX
      (H.264 7.3.2.3.1: last_payload_type_byte and last_payload_size_byte
      end the 0xFF runs); a header that overflowed was accepted, and
      the size wrapped. New FATE test fate-h264-sei-header.
    - FFmpeg pull request 25377 (https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/25377),
      patches 0071 to 0073: stereo3d keeps the eye order of interleaved
      columns (icr, icl:icr) and selects the right mono view of interleaved
      rows (irr:ml, irr:mr). New FATE tests filter-stereo3d-icr-sbsl,
      -irr-mono, -icr-sbsr and -icl-icr.
  * The changelog entry of +stereo3d11, which was never published, follows
    below with the source of +stereo3d9 as its base.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  @DATE@
